Caveat:  I'm still using Nethack 3.0 patchlevel 5, so if any of these
things have already been fixed, please ignore.

Complaints:

1.  Barbarians carrying entire hoards of treasure can squeeze through
cracks that wererats carrying a single item can't.  The ability to squeeze
through narrow cracks shouldn't be so proportional to your strength.

2.  There is a bug with the whatis command where sometimes things you can
see with telepathy are said to be "part of the floor or a ghost" (not
exact words).

Suggestions:

3.  When you pray, and your god isn't pleased, there should be a message
that gives you a hint as to what you've done wrong.  You should be able to
tell if you're praying too often or if you've really done something bad.
The penalty shouldn't be as severe if your god is displeased because
you've prayed too often.

4.  The whatis command (the `/' key) should not ask you any yes/no
questions.  It should immediately allow you to move the cursor around and
automatically identify any non-floor item under the cursor.  This would
encompass the functionality of the  directional look suggestion recently
posted.

Advice/spoilers:

5.  Always wish for "blessed" items (unless you specifically want a cursed
item).  Blessed armor or weapons are unlikely to be rusted or corroded,
and blessed potions and scrolls have more powerful effects.

6.  Wish for "gray dragon scale mail".  This stuff is awesome armor.  This
is the best base armor class you can get, it's rustproof, and it gives you
the same protection as a cloak of magic resistance, so you can wear some
other cloak instead.  With this armor, you can laugh at liches and nagas.

7.  You can get 6 wishes from a wand of wishing, not 3.  First wish for a
"blessed scroll of charging".  Then use two more wishes.  Then use the
scroll on the wand.  Then use three more wishes.  Now, the wand has 0
charges left, but if you try long enough, you can get one more wish out of
it.  I suggest engraving Elbereth in preparation.  Then give the zap
command a large repeat count like 200.  Just keep pressing the inventory
letter of your wand of wishing until it gives you a wish or you have to
stop to kill some monster.  Keep repeating this until you get your last wish.

8.  Wish for a wand of polymorph.  Collect big piles of stuff, including
rocks and worthless gems, and polymorph them.  Keep trying to get new
items and identify them.  If you have an altar handy, find the uncursed
and magic pieces of armor from monsters you have killed and polymorph them
until they are pieces you can wear.  I can usually find three or more +3
pieces of armor by the 10th level of the dungeon, mostly "black hats" from
orcs.  In a large group of soldiers, there will probably be a "+3 ring of
protection".  Keep that ring and polymorph all of the others.


